# Backend API base URL.
#
# Local development: leave this file alone and use .env.local. api.ts falls back
# to the current hostname on port 5008 when the value is localhost, which is what
# lets a phone on the booth Wi-Fi reach the dev machine without configuration.
#
# Vercel: set NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL in the project's Environment Variables,
# NOT in a committed file — it must be present at BUILD time because NEXT_PUBLIC_
# values are inlined into the bundle, so changing it needs a redeploy.
#
# No trailing slash: the client appends paths beginning with "/api/...".
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=https://tejooeloms.indusanalytics.co.in

# The customer-facing origin baked into every QR code and copied ordering
# link (see lib/utils.ts siteOrigin()). Leave unset locally — the QR then
# falls back to window.location.origin, which is what you want when testing
# from a phone on the venue Wi-Fi against a dev machine's LAN IP.
#
# MUST be set in Vercel (Production environment) to the real public domain.
# Without it, a QR generated while browsing a Vercel preview URL, a LAN IP,
# or localhost bakes that address into the code — the printed/downloaded QR
# does not fix itself once the mistake is noticed, every scan just fails.
# Same NEXT_PUBLIC_ build-time rule as above: changing it needs a redeploy.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://tejooeloms.indusanalytics.co.in
